<div class="section">
  <p class="eyebrow">Fit</p>
  <h2>Is this right for your family?</h2>

  <div class="fit">
    <div>
      <h3>This is probably right if</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your teen knows the material but underperforms under timed, high-stakes conditions</li>
        <li>You&rsquo;ve already tried tutoring or a prep course and the score hasn&rsquo;t moved</li>
        <li>Your teen will put in ten minutes a day on the practice, and show up each week</li>
        <li>You have roughly eight weeks before the target test date, and it lines up with a cohort start</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>It&rsquo;s probably not the right time if</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your teen has real content gaps. They need more foundation before state training will change much.</li>
        <li>Your teen isn&rsquo;t willing to engage with test prep at all. That&rsquo;s a motivation problem, and it comes before this one.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>We&rsquo;d rather say so on a call than take on a family this can&rsquo;t help.</p>
</div>

